			"Message": "style(Air): Enforce code formatting in ApplicationState module\n\nThis commit applies strict code formatting and variable naming normalization to the `Source/ApplicationState/mod.rs` file, continuing the hygiene standards enforced across the Air codebase in recent commits.\n\nSpecific adjustments include:\n- Converting all function arguments and local variables from `snake_case` to `PascalCase` (e.g., `connection_id` -> `ConnectionId`, `current_time` -> `CurrentTime`).\n- Updating method signatures and internal calls to reflect PascalCase naming (e.g., `initialize_service_status` -> `InitializeServiceStatus`).\n- Modifying utility calls to align with the capitalized naming convention (e.g., `utils::current_timestamp()` -> `utils::CurrentTimestamp()`).\n\nThis ensures the `ApplicationState` module, which manages the daemon's runtime health, connection pooling, and service lifecycle, adheres to the project's consistent style guide, minimizing visual noise in future diffs.",
