			"Message": "style(Air): Enforce code formatting in Downloader module\n\nThis commit applies strict code formatting and logic normalization to the `Source/Downloader/mod.rs` file, continuing the hygiene standards enforced across the Air codebase in recent commits.\n\nSpecific adjustments include:\n- Removing extraneous blank lines after import declarations.\n- Condensing `format!` macro arguments for error reporting, specifically within disk space validation logic.\n- Refactoring the `ExpectedChecksumFromConfig` helper to a concise single-line conditional expression.\n- Standardizing indentation for async closure chains, `if let` blocks, and long comment lines.\n- Updating variable names within `tokio::spawn` closures (e.g., `download_id` to `download_id_clone`, `did` to `_Did`) to ensure correct capture semantics and indicate intent.\n\nThis ensures the `Downloader` module, which handles the high-performance asset acquisition for the Land editor, adheres to the project's consistent style guide, minimizing visual noise and improving maintainability.",
			"SHA": "184c71ac7a0c6160d75e7f78b31e12687f374961"
