			"Message": "style(Air): Enforce code formatting in Daemon module\n\nThis commit applies strict code formatting and whitespace normalization to the `Source/Daemon/mod.rs` file, reinforcing the hygiene standards established in recent refactoring efforts.\n\nSpecific formatting adjustments include:\n- Removing spaces after colons in struct fields, function arguments, and variable type definitions (e.g., `name: Type` -> `name:Type`).\n- Condensing whitespace within generic angle brackets and function signatures.\n- Standardizing indentation and trailing commas for struct fields, match arms, and function bodies.\n- Alphabetically ordering import statements (`log`, `sha2`, `tokio`).\n- Reformatting docstring comments for consistent line width.\n\nThis ensures the `Daemon` module, which manages background process lifecycle and system service integration, adheres to the project's consistent style guide, minimizing visual noise in future diffs.",
			"SHA": "184267ad69a923083a9893c76ded4d6cd6c88d1d"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
