			"Message": "style(Air): Enforce code formatting in CLI module\n\nThis commit applies strict code formatting and whitespace normalization to the `Source/CLI/mod.rs` file, reinforcing the hygiene standards established in recent refactoring efforts.\n\nSpecific formatting adjustments include:\n- Removing spaces after colons in struct and field definitions (e.g., `name: Type` -> `name:Type`).\n- Condensing whitespace within generic angle brackets and function signatures.\n- Standardizing indentation and trailing commas for struct fields and match arms.\n- Consolidating import statements for better readability.\n\nThis ensures the `CLI` module, which serves as the primary interface for interacting with the Air daemon, adheres to the project's consistent style guide, minimizing visual noise in future diffs.",
